{"id":"U01","title":"Can We Turn Off Nightmares?","titleZh":"我们能关掉噩梦吗？","paras":[{"id":"U01-P1","sentences":[{"id":"U01-P1-S1","hard":false,"text":"The sheets are damp with sweat."},{"id":"U01-P1-S2","hard":true,"text":"You're cold, but your heart is racing as if a killer just chased you down a dark street."},{"id":"U01-P1-S3","hard":false,"text":"It was just a nightmare, you tell yourself; there's nothing to be afraid of."},{"id":"U01-P1-S4","hard":false,"text":"But you're still filled with fear."}]},{"id":"U01-P2","sentences":[{"id":"U01-P2-S1","hard":true,"text":"Given how unsettling and haunting nightmares can be, is there a way for dreamers to avoid, or even turn off, these bad dreams as they happen?"}]},{"id":"U01-P3","sentences":[{"id":"U01-P3-S1","hard":true,"text":"Research is limited, but some studies suggest that people who can master lucid dreaming—that is, the ability to be aware that a nightmare is happening and possibly even control it without waking up—may hold the answer."}]},{"id":"U01-P4","sentences":[{"id":"U01-P4-S1","hard":false,"text":"Nightmares are part of the human experience, especially for kids."},{"id":"U01-P4-S2","hard":false,"text":"Doctors typically don't consider occasional nightmares a problem."},{"id":"U01-P4-S3","hard":true,"text":"They can just be symptoms of a sleep disorder that can result from an unpleasant experience, stress, or certain drugs."}]},{"id":"U01-P5","sentences":[{"id":"U01-P5-S1","hard":true,"text":"To treat the disorder, there are a number of medicines and therapies that are backed by rigorous research, according to the American Academy of Sleep Medicine, which analyzed the available research on the treatment of nightmare disorder in a recent review published in the Journal of Clinical Sleep Medicine."}]},{"id":"U01-P6","sentences":[{"id":"U01-P6-S1","hard":true,"text":"However, nightmares are complicated, and researchers are still struggling to understand them, said Dr. Rachel Salas, an expert on sleep disorders and an associate professor at Johns Hopkins Medicine in Baltimore."},{"id":"U01-P6-S2","hard":true,"text":"What we do know is that people tend to have different kinds of nightmares at different points during the sleep cycle."}]}],"words":[{"id":"U01-W01","lemma":"sheet","surface":"sheets","pos":"n.","zh":"床单; 被单; (一)张(纸); 薄片","sent":"U01-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"a sheet of paper","zh":"一张纸"}]},{"id":"U01-W02","lemma":"damp","surface":"damp","pos":"adj.","zh":"潮湿的; 微湿的","sent":"U01-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"damp with sweat","zh":"被汗水浸湿"}]},{"id":"U01-W03","lemma":"sweat","surface":"sweat","pos":"n. / v.","zh":"n. 汗; 汗水 v. 出汗; 流汗","sent":"U01-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"in a cold sweat","zh":"出了一身冷汗"}]},{"id":"U01-W04","lemma":"race","surface":"racing","pos":"v. / n.","zh":"v. (心脏)狂跳; 快速运转; 参加比赛; 疾行 n. 比赛; 竞赛; 种族","sent":"U01-P1-S2","phrases":[{"en":"one's heart is racing","zh":"某人心跳加速"}]},{"id":"U01-W05","lemma":"chase","surface":"chased","pos":"v.","zh":"追赶; 追逐","sent":"U01-P1-S2","phrases":[{"en":"chase after","zh":"追赶; 追求"}]},{"id":"U01-W06","lemma":"nightmare","surface":"nightmare","pos":"n.","zh":"噩梦; 可怕的经历","sent":"U01-P1-S3","phrases":[{"en":"have a nightmare","zh":"做噩梦"}]},{"id":"U01-W07","lemma":"fill","surface":"filled","pos":"v.","zh":"(使)充满; 装满","sent":"U01-P1-S4","phrases":[{"en":"be filled with","zh":"充满"}]},{"id":"U01-W08","lemma":"fear","surface":"fear","pos":"n. / v.","zh":"n. 害怕; 恐惧 v. 害怕; 担心","sent":"U01-P1-S4","phrases":[{"en":"for fear of","zh":"以免; 唯恐"}]},{"id":"U01-W09","lemma":"given","surface":"Given","pos":"prep.","zh":"考虑到; 鉴于","sent":"U01-P2-S1","phrases":[{"en":"given that","zh":"考虑到; 鉴于"}]},{"id":"U01-W10","lemma":"unsettling","surface":"unsettling","pos":"adj.","zh":"令人不安的; 使人心神不宁的","sent":"U01-P2-S1","phrases":[]},{"id":"U01-W11","lemma":"haunting","surface":"haunting","pos":"adj.","zh":"萦绕心头的; 挥之不去的","sent":"U01-P2-S1","phrases":[]},{"id":"U01-W12","lemma":"dream","surface":"dreams","pos":"n. / v.","zh":"n. 梦; 梦想 v. 做梦; 梦想","sent":"U01-